    "ImageDescription": {
      "value": "The opening illustration by <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Willy_Pogany&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Willy Pogany (page does not exist)\">Willy Pogany</a> from the first chapter of <i>Children of Odin</i> entitled \"Far Away and Long Ago\". No title otherwise given for the work. The wolf <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Sk%C3%B6ll&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Sköll (page does not exist)\">Sköll</a> chases the personified sun, <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=S%C3%B3l_(Sun)&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Sól (Sun) (page does not exist)\">Sól</a>, and his brother <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Hati_Hr%C3%B3%C3%B0vitnisson&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Hati Hróðvitnisson (page does not exist)\">Hati Hróðvitnisson</a> chases the personified moon, <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=M%C3%A1ni&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Máni (page does not exist)\">Máni</a>, from <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Norse_mythology&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Norse mythology (page does not exist)\">Norse mythology</a>.",
      "source": "commons-desc-page"
    },
    "Credit": {
      "value": "Originally from <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Padraic_Colum&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Padraic Colum (page does not exist)\">Colum, Padraic</a> (1920). <i>The Children of Odin</i>. New York: <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=The_Macmillan_Company&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"The Macmillan Company (page does not exist)\">The Macmillan Company</a>. Illustrated by Pogany, Willy. As found at <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"http://www.mainlesson.com/display.php?author=colum&amp;book=odin&amp;story=_contents\">http://www.mainlesson.com/display.php?author=colum&amp;book=odin&amp;story=_contents</a>",
